SHADER PIPELINE

I'll be honest, I've got barely a clue how to *actually* work with shaders.
I did play around enough in blender's post-processing though to roughly
know how to do things in theory. Or in other words: I can come up with a
pipeline (as I think it's called at least).

1. BLOOMY COLORATION

1) Render scene as pure black and white (or maybe grayscale).
2) Gaussian-blur that with a very large gaussian.
3) Add the blurred render to the normal render to get a bloom effect. Keep
   the maximum brightness as 2.0 though, not 1.0.
4) Interpolate between black, a tint and white based on the brightness. A
   brightness of 0.0 is black, 1.0 is the tint, 2.0 is white.
